cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this study's software or results, please cite this repository.
  Original template attribution is retained in
  docs/CAIDS_TEMPLATE_CITATION.cff.
type: software
title: >-
  An Interpretable Machine Learning Framework for Analysing
  Learner Engagement Patterns in E-Learning Environments
authors:
  - given-names: Carol Mwaba
    family-names: Chiyassa
    affiliation: University of South Africa
abstract: >-
  An OULAD study comparing logistic regression, Explainable Boosting
  Machines, and XGBoost for academic-risk prediction using learner
  characteristics and activity from days 0–30 inclusive. Evaluation
  includes learner-separated validation, held-out testing, permutation
  importance, paired learner bootstrap comparisons, and five-seed
  predictive stability analysis.
keywords:
  - learning analytics
  - OULAD
  - academic risk
  - interpretable machine learning
  - reproducible research